cat >> /home/claude/notes/findings.md << 'EOF'

## CONFIRMED HIGH: node-agent workspace cleanup route references undefined `path`/`fs` -> always fails -> disk space leak

File: services/node-agent/src/index.js, `DELETE /agent/fs/:deploymentId/cleanup` (~line 489)
```js
app.delete('/agent/fs/:deploymentId/cleanup', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const dir = path.join(WORKSPACES_DIR, req.params.deploymentId);
    if (fs.existsSync(dir)) { fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }); }
    res.json({ ok: true });
  } catch (err) { res.status(500).json({ error: err.message }); }
});
```
Neither `path` nor `fs` (node's built-in modules) are ever `require()`d at the top of index.js (only
`fs` is separately required *inline*, scoped to a different, unrelated handler around line 795/827 --
that local `const fs = require('fs')` does not leak into this handler's scope). Every call to this route
throws `ReferenceError: path is not defined`, caught by the try/catch, returning HTTP 500 with
`{ error: "path is not defined" }`.

Caller: apps/api/src/jobs/workspace-cleanup.ts (`executeWorkspaceCleanupJob`, run on a schedule -- check
worker.ts for the cron trigger) calls this endpoint for every non-Git deployment (zip://, upload:// repos)
older than 24h. Since `res.ok` is always false, the job only ever logs
`'Node workspace cleanup endpoint returned error'` and never sets `workspaceCleanedAt`, so the same
deployments are retried (and fail) on every sweep, forever. Net effect: workspace directories for
zip/manual-upload deployments are never purged from node disks -- a permanent, silent disk-space leak on
every node, with no user-facing error (it's a background job).

Severity: HIGH (silent resource leak, will eventually fill node disks; trivial one-line fix).
EOF
echo done

